{
  "id": "neural-synchrony",
  "term": "neural synchrony",
  "definition": "Neural synchrony is the matching or similarity of neural activity patterns between people during interaction, used as a biological sign of how closely they are aligning cognitively and socially. In the source packet, it refers specifically to interbrain similarity measured from EEG signals during naturalistic dialogue or a shared task.",
